    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Innovators at Pakistan's first-ever medical hackathon at the Aga Khan University have proposed new ways of tackling challenges facing Pakistan's emergency rooms (ER). HistorER , the winning team at the Hackathon, came up with a unique QR (quick response) code system to address a persistent challenge faced by ER doctors. Patients are often brought to emergency by family members or by bystanders who are not aware of their medical history. In the absence of critical information, doctors face delays in performing life-saving procedures.",
